```

For example, given the array `arr = [1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13]` and the target `target = 7`, the function should return `3` as the index of the target in the array.

### Solution:
```java
public static int modifiedBinarySearch(int[] arr, int n, int target) {
    int s = 0, e = n - 1;
    while (s <= e) {
        int mid = s + (e - s) / 2;
        if (arr[mid] == target) {
            return mid;
        } else {
            if (arr[mid] < target && arr[e] >= target) {
                s = mid + 1;
            } else {
                e = mid - 1;
            }
        }
    }
    return -1;
}
