### Problem:
You are tasked with implementing a simplified version of a visitor pattern for an abstract syntax tree (AST) representing mathematical expressions. The AST consists of binary and unary expressions, as well as literal values. Your goal is to create a visitor that can evaluate the value of the AST based on the given expression.

You are provided with the following classes:

```java
public abstract class Expression {
    public abstract void accept(ExpressionVisitor visitor);
}

public class BinaryExpression extends Expression {
    private Expression left;
    private Expression right;
    private char operator;

    public BinaryExpression(Expression left, Expression right, char operator) {
        this.left = left;
        this.right = right;
        this.operator = operator;
    }

    public Expression getLeft() {
        return left;
    }

    public Expression getRight() {
        return right;
    }

