public class UnaryExpression extends Expression {
    private Expression expression;
    private char operator;

    public UnaryExpression(Expression expression, char operator) {
        this.expression = expression;
        this.operator = operator;
    }

    public Expression getExpression() {
        return expression;
    }

    public char getOperator() {
        return operator;
    }

    @Override
    public void accept(ExpressionVisitor visitor) {
        visitor.visitUnaryExpression(this);
    }
}

public class Literal extends Expression {
    private double value;

    public Literal(double value) {
        this.value = value;
    }

    public double getValue() {
        return value;
    }

    @Override
    public void accept(ExpressionVisitor visitor) {
        visitor.visitLiteral(this);
    }
}

public interface ExpressionVisitor {
    void visitBinaryExpression(BinaryExpression expression);
    void visitUnaryExpression(UnaryExpression expression);
    void visitLiteral(Literal literal);
}
```

Your task is to implement a concrete `ExpressionVisitor` that evaluates the value of the AST. The visitor should traverse the AST and perform the necessary operations to compute the final result based on the given expression.

Write a Java class `Evaluator` that implements the `ExpressionVisitor` interface and provides the logic to evaluate the AST.

### Solution:
```java
public class Evaluator implements ExpressionVisitor {
    private double result;

    public double evaluate(Expression expression) {
        expression.accept(this);
        return result;
    }

    @Override
    public void visitBinaryExpression(BinaryExpression expression) {
        expression.getLeft().accept(this);
        double leftValue = result;
        expression.getRight().accept(this);
        double rightValue = result;

        char operator = expression.getOperator();
        switch (operator) {
            case '+':
                result = leftValue + rightValue;
                break;
            case '-':
                result = leftValue - rightValue;
                break;
            case '*':
                result = leftValue * rightValue;
                break;
            case '/':
                result = leftValue / rightValue;
                break;
            // Handle other operators as needed
        }
    }

    @Override
    public void visitUnaryExpression(UnaryExpression expression) {
        expression.getExpression().accept(this);
        double value = result;

        char operator = expression.getOperator();
        switch (operator) {
            case '-':
                result = -value;
                break;
            // Handle other unary operators as needed
        }
    }

    @Override
    public void visitLiteral(Literal literal) {
        result = literal.getValue();
    }
}
```

